-- title:
--   Qxp Proj Sub Meas Total Eq X Hat Adjoint Mul X Hat
-- statement:
--   **The Q/X/XHat/P projective total is the Gram operator of XHat.**
--
--   Let `data` be a Q/X/XHat/P layer package on a finite Hilbert space with finite outcome set. Its auxiliary projective measurement has effects $T_a$, and the canonical projective submeasurement has outcome operators
--
--   $$
--   P_a=\widehat X^{\dagger}T_a\widehat X.
--   $$
--
--   The total operator stored by this projective submeasurement is the Gram operator of $\widehat X$:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_a P_a=\widehat X^{\dagger}\widehat X.
--   $$
--
--   Equivalently, the `total` field of the canonical QXP projective submeasurement, viewed as a submeasurement total, equals `data.xHat` adjoint-multiplied by itself. This is the total-mass identity used in later comparisons between the repaired projective family and its source family.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.qxpProjSubMeas_total_eq_xHat_adjoint_mul_xHat`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
